# Specifications, editable diagram data and coverage are all authored before comparison.
def emit():
    for v in VIEWS:
        key=v['id']; p=OUT/'architecture'/f'{key}.md'
        lines=[f'# {v["title"]}', '',f'Owner: `{v["owner"]}`. Granularity: {v["kind"]}.', '',
               f'Scope and boundaries: {v["scope"]}.','',
               f'[SVG](../diagrams/svg/{key}.svg) · [Editable JSON](../diagrams/source/{key}.json) · [Coverage](../baseline/coverage.md) · [Baseline](../baseline/index.md)','',
               '## Responsibilities and implementation evidence','', '| Level | Claim | Evidence |','| --- | --- | --- |']
        for c in v['claims']:
            e=v['evidence'][c['evidence']-1]
            lines.append(f'| {c["classification"]} | {c["statement"]} | E{c["evidence"]}: {link(e)} |')
        lines+=['','## Interfaces and flow','', '| Edge | Producer / caller | Consumer / target | Meaning | Evidence |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
        names={n['id']:n['label'] for n in v['nodes']}
        for i,e in enumerate(v['edges'],1):
            lines.append(f'| E{i} | {names[e["from"]]} | {names[e["to"]]} | {e["type"]}: {e["label"]} | Claim E{e["evidence"]} above |')
        lines+=['','## Limits','',v['limits'] or 'Static source trace only. Runtime behavior, scale and interoperability have not been verified.', '',
                'The diagram is a selected architecture view, not a complete call graph. Component ownership is the outer frame; process, storage and external nodes are explicitly labeled. Edge styles follow the [shared notation](../diagrams/notation.md).', '',
                'Related: [flows](../baseline/lifecycles.md), [data and contracts](../baseline/data-contracts.md), [inputs and extension points](../baseline/inputs-extensions.md), [engineering](../baseline/engineering.md).']
        p.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
        (OUT/'diagrams/source'/f'{key}.json').write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
    lines=['# Coverage matrix','','This matrix covers every discovered workspace package and the major components defined below. **Traced** means architectural responsibilities and the listed boundary flows were inspected in source; it does not mean every line or branch was audited. **Mapped** source files in the census are accounted for but not all individually read. Tests are supporting/declaration evidence only.','','Granularity: a major component owns a cohesive service, lifecycle, protocol boundary, persistence family or UI surface family. Closely related helpers remain in their owning component; a file is not automatically a component. Package views show internal families; linked detailed views expand substantial subsystems.','','| ID | Inventory item | Owner | Status | Specification / source evidence | SVG | Editable source |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
    for v in VIEWS:
        k=v['id']; status='Partial implementation, traced' if k=='integration-t3code' else 'Traced; static only'
        lines.append(f'| `{k}` | {v["title"]} | `{v["owner"]}` | {status} | [Specification](../architecture/{k}.md) | [SVG](../diagrams/svg/{k}.svg) | [JSON](../diagrams/source/{k}.json) |')
    lines+=['','All 11 `packages/*` and both `tools/*` workspace manifests are represented. Non-package executable/deployment assets are covered by delivery and workflow-assets. [File census](source-census.tsv) records 614 non-document tracked files with hashes; [package dependency inventory](dependencies.md) distinguishes manifest dependency kinds. [Source map](source-map.md) expands file-level ownership and inspected test declarations.','','Unresolved evidence and explicitly absent/unverified categories are in [uncertainties](uncertainties.md). Diagram sources contain claim-level evidence records. No record asserts runtime pass/fail.']
    (OUT/'baseline/coverage.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    (OUT/'diagrams/notation.md').write_text('''# Diagram notation

Every view has an editable JSON source, SVG and architecture specification. Sources list actual named nodes, typed labeled edges, claims and concrete source evidence. JSON is the editable graph format; no external renderer is needed.

- The outer frame denotes package/component ownership for this view, not a claim that every displayed external dependency is inside that package.
- Each node states its role: component, process, boundary, interface, data, message, storage, external. Explicit process and external boxes identify process/trust crossings; a dependency alone is not a security boundary.
- Solid blue: call. Dashed purple: dependency. Dotted green: event/message. Thick brown: data movement. Gray: containment. Dashed red: declared/unimplemented edge.
- Arrows show direction. For bidirectional transports, the label names the exchange. Numbered edge badges connect to the full source → target and operation table below the graph; the table is part of the diagram, so no arrow is unlabeled.
- Storage boxes denote persisted data, except where a node explicitly says memory. “Data” denotes a value, not necessarily persistence.

The rail layout keeps labeled interfaces legible without crossing text. It intentionally favors traceability over a physical deployment map. The system view names process boundaries; package and component views refine ownership. Every diagram is a static interpretation of the linked code, never runtime observation.

[Baseline index](../baseline/index.md) · [Coverage / complete view list](../baseline/coverage.md)
''')
if __name__=='__main__':emit()
